https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OYIjLs6tpwo  (Capo 0)

TIP:  The whole song is just (G) (C) (D) with a strumming pattern that has a two-count on each chord.  The best way to play it is to attack the root note with the first strum.  So for the sequence it would be covered top string <g>/strum (G); covered 5th string <c>/strum (C), and open 4th <d>/strum (D).  Or simply hit the top three strings with an abbreviated down stroke on the first beat of the chord followed by a full strum of the same chord.

TIP:  In the verse the (D) sometimes comes on a downstroke following the preceding word as Raul briefly pauses before progressing to the following word.  You'll hear it when you play.

TIP:  Raul sings the last verse in Spanish but there's a loose translation in English included.
   
          
